---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StrategyFunds from '../../../../components/StrategyFunds.astro';
import { STAT } from '../../../../data/aif-facts';
---
<BaseLayout currentPage="knowledge/aif">

<div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-10 lg:px-12 pb-24">

  <!-- Breadcrumb -->
  <nav class="py-6 flex items-center gap-2 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-widest font-bold text-outline border-b border-outline-variant/20 flex-wrap">
    <a href="/knowledge/aif" class="hover:text-secondary transition-colors">AIF Knowledge</a>
    <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sm text-outline-variant">chevron_right</span>
    <a href="/knowledge/aif/category-ii" class="hover:text-secondary transition-colors">Category II AIF</a>
    <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sm text-outline-variant">chevron_right</span>
    <span class="text-on-surface-variant">Debt Funds</span>
  </nav>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20 border-b border-outline-variant/20 mb-16">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-end">
      <div class="md:col-span-8">
        <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-secondary font-bold mb-3 block">Category II AIF · SEBI AIF Regulations, 2012</span>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4 flex-wrap">
          <span class="text-[10px] px-3 py-1.5 bg-secondary text-surface uppercase font-bold tracking-widest">Category II</span>
          <span class="text-[10px] px-3 py-1.5 bg-surface-container text-secondary border border-outline-variant/30 uppercase font-bold tracking-widest">Private Debt</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-7xl font-headline text-primary-container leading-tight mb-6">
          Debt <span class="italic font-light">Funds</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          Category II AIF Debt Funds provide structured private credit to mid-market Indian companies through NCDs, mezzanine instruments, and secured lending solutions — delivering predictable yield of 12–18% p.a. against collateral packages in a pass-through tax framework.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-4">
        <div class="bg-secondary p-8">
          <span class="text-[10px] uppercase font-bold tracking-widest text-surface/70 block mb-4">Key Criteria</span>
          <ul class="space-y-3">
            {[
              'Senior secured NCDs & mezzanine debt',
              'Target yield: 12–18% p.a.',
              'Collateral: promoter pledge, charge on assets',
              'No leverage at fund level permitted',
              'Pass-through taxation under Sec. 224, IT Act 2025',
            ].map(item => (
              <li class="text-sm text-surface font-medium flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[14px] mt-0.5 shrink-0">check_circle</span>{item}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Definition -->
  <section class="mb-16 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-10">
    <div class="md:col-span-5 bg-surface-container-low p-10">
      <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl text-primary-container mb-6">SEBI Definition</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-loose">
        Category II AIF Debt Funds invest primarily in debt and debt-linked instruments of unlisted companies. They do not employ leverage or borrowing (other than for operational purposes up to 10 days). Unlike bank credit, AIF debt is privately negotiated, structured, and can be tailored to company-specific cash flow profiles with flexible tenures and covenants.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 pt-8 border-t border-outline-variant/30">
        <span class="text-[10px] font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-outline">Governing Regulation</span>
        <p class="font-headline text-lg text-primary-container mt-1">SEBI AIF Regs, 2012 – Reg 3(4)(b)</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="md:col-span-7">
      <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl text-primary-container mb-6">India's Private Credit Opportunity</h2>
      <p class="text-base text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed mb-5">
        India's mid-market (₹100 Cr – ₹2,000 Cr revenue companies) faces a structural credit gap. Banks are constrained by NPA concerns, collateral norms, and sector-level limits; public bond markets require credit ratings and large issuance sizes. AIF Debt Funds fill this gap by providing bespoke, relatively rapid credit to quality mid-market borrowers at higher-than-bank rates, with strong collateral coverage.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
        India's private credit AIF market has grown rapidly, with global managers (Ares, KKR Credit, Cerberus) and domestic managers (IIFL, Piramal, Kotak) deploying capital. The sector benefits from India's economic growth, formalisation of corporate borrowing, and the retrenchment of NBFCs from mid-market lending after the IL&FS crisis.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Debt Structures -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="font-headline text-4xl text-primary-container mb-2">Debt Instrument Types</h2>
    <div class="w-12 h-1 bg-secondary mb-10"></div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
      {[
        { icon: 'security', title: 'Senior Secured NCDs', desc: 'Non-Convertible Debentures with first or second charge on company assets (plant, land, receivables). Highest in repayment priority. Typically yield 13–15% p.a. with 2–4 year tenure.' },
        { icon: 'stairs', title: 'Mezzanine Debt', desc: 'Subordinated debt ranking behind senior secured lenders but ahead of equity. Often includes equity kickers (warrants or CCPS) to enhance total returns. Yields 15–18% p.a. with higher risk profile.' },
        { icon: 'payments', title: 'Structured Receivables', desc: 'Financing against contracted future receivables — government receivables, export proceeds, or escrow-backed cash flows. Short-duration, self-liquidating structures with strong asset coverage.' },
        { icon: 'real_estate_agent', title: 'Real Estate Debt', desc: 'Construction finance and last-mile funding for residential projects. RERA registration, sales velocity data, and cash flow escrows provide security. Typically 12–16% yield with 18–36 month tenure.' },
        { icon: 'agriculture', title: 'Agri & MSME Credit', desc: 'Structured credit to agri-processors, MSME exporters, and supply chain financing vehicles. Government-backed schemes (MSME Udyam, RBI TLTRO) enhance credit quality of underlying borrowers.' },
        { icon: 'account_tree', title: 'Promoter Financing', desc: 'Loans against promoter pledge of listed shares or other high-quality collateral. Short-duration, high-yield (14–18%) with conservative LTV (50–60%) for collateral coverage.' },
      ].map(step => (
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 border border-outline-variant/10">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-secondary text-3xl mb-4 block">{step.icon}</span>
          <h3 class="font-headline text-xl text-primary-container mb-3">{step.title}</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">{step.desc}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Key Characteristics -->
  <section class="mb-16 bg-primary-container text-surface px-8 md:px-12 py-12 relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-64 h-64 bg-secondary/10 rounded-full blur-3xl translate-x-1/3 -translate-y-1/3 pointer-events-none"></div>
    <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl text-tertiary-fixed mb-10 relative z-10">Key <span class="italic">Characteristics at a Glance</span></h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4 relative z-10">
      {[
        STAT.minCorpus,
        STAT.minTicket,
        STAT.closeEnded,
        { label: 'Typical Tenure',       value: '3–5 Years',         sub: 'from final close' },
        STAT.noLeverage,
        { label: 'Target Yield',         value: '12–18% p.a.',       sub: 'gross, indicative' },
        STAT.passThrough,
        { label: 'TDS on Fund Income',   value: '10% (residents)',   sub: 'Sec. 393(1), IT Act 2025' },
      ].map(p => (
        <div class="border border-secondary/30 p-5">
          <p class="text-[10px] uppercase font-label tracking-wider text-slate-400 mb-1">{p.label}</p>
          <p class="font-headline text-xl text-tertiary-fixed leading-tight">{p.value}</p>
          <p class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 mt-1">{p.sub}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Risk Factors -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="font-headline text-4xl text-primary-container mb-6">Risk Considerations</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      {[
        { icon: 'credit_score', title: 'Credit / Default Risk', desc: 'Borrower default or delayed repayment is the primary risk. Collateral enforcement in India can take 2–5 years through DRT/SARFAESI — post-default recovery is uncertain and time-consuming.' },
        { icon: 'lock', title: 'Illiquidity', desc: 'AIF debt instruments have no secondary market. If a borrower delays repayment, the fund\'s tenure may extend beyond the planned exit horizon, trapping capital.' },
        { icon: 'account_balance', title: 'Collateral Enforcement Risk', desc: 'Real estate or asset-backed collateral values can decline in downturns. Promoter pledges are subject to market price risk for listed share collateral.' },
        { icon: 'policy', title: 'Concentration Risk', desc: 'Many debt AIFs have concentrated exposures (5–8 borrowers). A single large default can materially impact NAV. Diversification across borrowers and structures is essential.' },
      ].map(r => (
        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 border border-outline-variant/10 flex gap-4">
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-secondary text-2xl shrink-0 mt-0.5">{r.icon}</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-primary-container mb-2">{r.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">{r.desc}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="bg-primary-container text-white px-10 md:px-16 py-12 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-start md:items-center justify-between gap-8 relative overflow-hidden mb-12">
    <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-64 h-64 bg-secondary/10 rounded-full blur-3xl translate-x-1/3 -translate-y-1/3 pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="max-w-lg relative z-10">
      <h2 class="font-headline text-3xl text-amber-100 mb-2">Explore Private Debt Opportunities</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Access SEBI-registered Category II Debt AIFs through Platizio Alternatives's institutional platform.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 relative z-10">
      <a href="/explore" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-tertiary-fixed text-on-tertiary-fixed px-8 py-4 text-[11px] uppercase font-bold tracking-widest hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity">
        Browse Funds <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sm">arrow_forward</span>
      </a>
      <button type="button" class="js-open-consult inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-white/30 text-white px-8 py-4 text-[11px] uppercase font-bold tracking-widest hover:bg-white/10 transition-colors cursor-pointer">
        Speak to Advisor
      </button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Prev / Next -->
  <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
    <a href="/knowledge/aif/category-ii/private-equity" class="flex-1 border border-outline p-5 hover:border-secondary transition-colors group text-center">
      <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-outline block mb-1">Previous</span>
      <span class="font-headline text-lg text-primary-container group-hover:text-secondary transition-colors">Private Equity Funds</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/knowledge/aif/category-ii/real-estate" class="flex-1 border border-outline p-5 hover:border-secondary transition-colors group text-center">
      <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-outline block mb-1">Next</span>
      <span class="font-headline text-lg text-primary-container group-hover:text-secondary transition-colors">Real Estate Funds</span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <StrategyFunds sub="debt" label="Debt Funds" />

</div>
</BaseLayout>
